# Fallow — Codebase Hygiene

This rule applies **only when Fallow is installed** in the workspace: a `fallow` binary on PATH, a `fallow` devDependency, or a `dead-code:audit` package script. If none of those exist, skip Fallow steps and note that they were skipped — do not install Fallow, and do not substitute knip, jscpd, or parallel dead-code tools.

## When to run

| Situation | Command |
|-----------|---------|
| After substantial TS/JS changes | the repo's dead-code audit script (e.g. `bun run dead-code:audit`) or `fallow audit --format json` |
| Before deleting exports/files | `fallow inspect --symbol <file>:<export>` |
| Duplication / overlap suspicion | `fallow dupes --trace <file>:<line>` |
| Full hygiene scan | the repo's full dead-code script (e.g. `bun run dead-code`) |
| CI regression gate | the repo's dead-code check script (e.g. `bun run dead-code:check`) |

## Agent workflow

1. Edit code
2. Run the dead-code audit (script or `fallow audit --format json` for structured output)
3. Fix introduced findings; prefer deletion over suppression
4. Do not increase the dead-code regression baseline without intentional cleanup

Before merge on substantial bug/feature work, run **`/vsd-code-review`** (this plugin's `skills/vsd-code-review/SKILL.md`) — thermo-nuclear structure audit, KISS/YAGNI pass, Fallow checks, deslop audit, and test bar in one shot. Use `/vsd-code-review rerun` after fixes to score prior blockers. Run **`/deslop`** separately to auto-remove AI slop from the branch diff.

## Config

Project config: `.fallowrc.jsonc`. Baselines live in `regression.baseline` — update only when intentionally paying down debt, never when adding dead code.

## MCP & editor

- MCP: repos may wire `fallow-mcp` into `.cursor/mcp.json` (trace imports, inspect targets, audit JSON)
- VS Code extension: `fallow-rs.fallow-vscode`

